{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "target" %}
{# render_mode guard MUST be within the first 5 lines (see 0330). #}
{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{# Relationships - the officiant (2.5, Build A; spec 5.3, 5.4)                  #}
{#                                                                            #}
{# Any priest, priestess or jarl can marry the player to their betrothed,      #}
{# here and now, unplanned. Officiants are seldom enrolled, so 0330 never       #}
{# reaches them: this tells them only when it matters - someone engaged to the #}
{# player is here with them. Silent otherwise. get_officiant is native.        #}
{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{% if not is_player(actorUUID) %}
{% if is_plugin_loaded("SNRom_Integration.esl") %}
{% set off = get_officiant(actorUUID) %}
{# THE WEDDING YOU ARE CONDUCTING (Ceremony.h), by step: 1 you have opened and
   asked the player, 2 the player said yes and you ask the betrothed, 3 both
   said yes and you pronounce them married. The author, 2026-10-20: spoken
   like a real wedding, one question at a time, and nobody married until both
   have said yes and you declare it. #}
{% if off and default(off.officiant, 0) == 1 and default(off.ceremony, 0) > 0 %}
{% set them = default(off.marrying, "your betrothed") %}

## The Wedding You Are Conducting

You are marrying {{ player.name }} and {{ them }}, now, here, before whoever is present. It is a wedding, not a chat: speak as one who marries people, with the solemnity and warmth that are yours, and let each of them answer for themselves.
{% if off.ceremony == 1 %}
You have begun. Say a few words fitting the moment if you have not, then ask {{ player.name }}, plainly, whether they take {{ them }} to be their {% if default(off.marryingFemale, 0) == 1 %}wife{% else %}husband{% endif %} - and wait for their answer. Do not answer for them, and do not ask {{ them }} yet.
{% elif off.ceremony == 2 %}
{{ player.name }} has said yes. Now ask {{ them }} whether they take {{ player.name }}, and let {{ them }} answer for themselves. Do not pronounce anything yet.
{% elif off.ceremony == 3 %}
Both {{ player.name }} and {{ them }} have said yes. Pronounce them married, in your own words.
{% endif %}
{% elif off and default(off.officiant, 0) == 1 and existsIn(off, "betrothed") and length(off.betrothed) > 0 %}

## Who Has Come Before You

{{ player.name }} is here with {% for name in off.betrothed %}{{ name }}{% if not loop.is_last %} and {% endif %}{% endfor %}, to whom they are engaged. As one who can marry people, you could marry them here and now, if they ask you and you are willing: a few words fitting the moment, then you ask each of them in turn whether they take the other, and when both have said yes, you pronounce them married. Whether you would is yours to judge, as yourself.
{% if default(off.mayMarry, 1) == 0 %}
But {{ player.name }} is already married, and Mara has granted them no exception. You know it, and you will not marry them to another. Say so in your own way.
{% elif default(off.exception, 0) == 1 and default(off.spouses, 0) > 0 %}
{{ player.name }} holds Mara's own exception to marry more than once. Every priest knows it; you may still have an opinion.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
